t observation about Sasha, and whether the essay's reading holds the other input's node at its prior.\n\nI'm settling on submitting the letter: the essay's 6.3 case, with different observations, holds the other copy's node at its prior, so defecting dominates here.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9823,"completion_tokens":967,"total_tokens":10790,"cost":0.058632,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.058632,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039292,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01934},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":607,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}